# index-fixed-decl: Does a constant index on a declared name name the numbered symbol (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: s=14 w=3 e=40 m=18
# pc: ok
# states: 3
# ruling: pc-ode reads `name[n]` on the left of a fixed quantity, `y[n]'`, `dy[n]/dt`, `par`, `init`, `number`, `!`, `aux`, `table`, a function line and a `%[i1..i2]` block as the declaration of `name<n>` (language.md, Arrays).
y[1]'=1
dz[2]/dt=2
q2'=0
y1(0)=0
z2(0)=0
init q[2]=4
par a[2]=3
number n[2]=6
f[3]=7
!d[2]=n2+1
g[2](u)=u*4
table h[2] % 3 0 2 t^2
aux s=f3+a2+g2(1)+y[1]+z[2]
aux w[2]=y1+3
aux e=d2+h2(1)+q[2]+g2(f[3])
%[1..2]
v[j]=n[2]*[j]
%
aux m=v[2]+v1
@ total=0,dt=1
